                     --repro "<how to make it happen again: the command or the steps>"
                     [--details TEXT | --details -]   the whole story (stdin with -): what you did, what
                                                      you saw, what you expected, how you got around it
                     [--evidence PATH] [--by ROLE]
          KIND: refused | broken-tool | flaky-check | unclear-rule | slow | other
          AREA: what it's in - ship, gate, verify, board, comms, permissions, worktree, phone, apk, ...
          --repro is required: "none: <why it can't be reproduced>" when there's really no way.
          --fixed SHA: logging one that's already fixed (a record of it; it reopens if it comes back).
  powos friction list [--all] [--fixed] [--area A] [--id ID ...] [--json]   open ones, most frequent first
                     --id: just these ids (repeatable) - a cluster's status in one call, not the whole dump
  powos friction show <id>                     one, whole (details, repro, evidence)
  powos friction fix <id> --commit SHA [--note TEXT]   fixed for good; logged again later, it reopens
  powos friction link <id> <task|->            the task it is evidence for (also: add --task, task set --friction
                                               f30,f31): its count feeds the task's severity
Severity (a task's, from its evidence): score = linked friction reports x1 + the user's "still broken" verdicts x50
+ repeated asks (each linked ask past the first) x25; P1 at 50, P0 at 500; only ever raised. Recomputed by the
module on every friction add/link, verdict and ask link, and by each board sweep. Closing a task as done marks its
linked friction fixed; only a cancel (task rm) reopens it; a merge moves it to the target. One-off friction unseen
7 days goes quiet (out of the live list, --all shows it) and is open again when logged again.

Tools log their own: a ship refusal or failure (ship.sh), a shell gate failure under Mac load (gate.sh),
an INVALID or SKIPPED phone check (queue.sh), a permission refusal of an agent's tool call (powos-agentsd).
Off the phone (the Mac): python3 lib/ai/agents/powos-agents-cli friction ...  (tools/agents/friction).
"""


def friction_cmd(argv):
    verb = argv[0] if argv else "list"
    argv = argv[1:]
    if verb in ("help", "--help", "-h"):
        print(FRICTION_HELP, end="")
    elif verb == "add":
        friction_add(argv)
    elif verb == "link":
        if len(argv) != 2:
            die("usage: powos friction link <id> <task|->   (the task it is evidence for; - unlinks)")
        call("friction_link", argv[0], "" if argv[1] == "-" else find(argv[1])["id"])
        print(f"{argv[0]} -> {argv[1]}")
    elif verb == "fix":
        o, rest = opts(argv, ["commit", "note"])
        if len(rest) != 1 or not o.get("commit"):
            die("usage: powos friction fix <id> --commit SHA [--note TEXT]")
        sha = git_commits([o["commit"]])[0]["sha"] if re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-fA-F]{4,40}", o["commit"]) else die("--commit takes a sha")
        call("friction_fix", rest[0], sha, o.get("note", ""))
        print(rest[0])
    elif verb == "show":
        f = next((x for x in table("friction") if x["id"] in argv), None) or die(f"no friction {' '.join(argv)!r}")
        for k in ("id", "status", "area", "kind", "title", "count", "reopened", "by", "repro", "evidence", "details",
                  "fix_commit", "fix_note"):
            if f.get(k) not in ("", 0, None) or k in ("repro",):
                print(f"{k}: {f[k]}")
        print(f"first: {ago(int(f['first']))} ago, last: {ago(int(f['last']))} ago")
    elif verb in ("list", "ls"):
        o, _ = opts(argv, ["all!", "fixed!", "area", "id*", "json!", "full!"])
        ids = set(o.get("id") or [])
        want = "fixed" if o.get("fixed") else "open"   # live = open; quiet ones (one-off, unseen 7 days): --all
        fs = [f for f in table("friction") if (ids or o.get("all") or f["status"] == want)
              and (not o.get("area") or f["area"] == o["area"]) and (not ids or f["id"] in ids)]
        fs.sort(key=lambda f: (-int(f["count"]), -int(f["last"])))
        more = 0
        if not (o.get("all") or o.get("full") or ids) and len(fs) > LIST_MAX:
            more, fs = len(fs) - LIST_MAX, fs[:LIST_MAX]
        if not o.get("full"):
            fs = [dict(f, details=cut_body(f.get("details")), repro=cut_body(f.get("repro"))) for f in fs]
        if o.get("json"):
            print(json.dumps(fs, indent=1))
            return
        if not fs:
            print("no friction logged" if not o.get("fixed") else "nothing fixed yet")
        for f in fs:
            fixed = f"  fixed {f['fix_commit'][:9]}" if f["status"] == "fixed" else ""
            back = f"  reopened x{f['reopened']}" if int(f.get("reopened") or 0) else ""
            quiet = "  quiet" if f["status"] == "quiet" else ""
            on = f"  -> {f['task']}" if f.get("task") else ""
            print(f"{f['id']:<5} x{f['count']:<3} [{f['area']}/{f['kind']}] {f['title']}  ({ago(int(f['last']))} ago){fixed}{back}{quiet}{on}")
            if f.get("repro"):
                print(f"            repro: {_line(f['repro'])[:150]}")
        if more:
            print(f"... {more} more (--all)")
    else:
        die(f"unknown: friction {verb} (powos friction help)")


def friction_add(argv):
    o, rest = opts(argv, ["area", "kind", "repro", "details", "evidence", "by", "fixed", "task"])
    title = " ".join(rest).strip()
    if not title or not o.get("area") or not o.get("kind"):
        die('usage: powos friction add --area AREA --kind KIND "<title>" --repro "<how to reproduce>" [--details TEXT|-]')
    if o["kind"] not in FRICTION_KINDS:
        die(f"--kind is one of {' | '.join(FRICTION_KINDS)}")
    if not (o.get("repro") or "").strip():
        die('--repro is required (the command or steps that make it happen again; "none: <why>" if there is no way)')
    details = o.get("details", "")
    item = {"area": o["area"], "kind": o["kind"], "title": title, "details": details, "repro": o["repro"],
            "evidence": o.get("evidence", ""), "by": o.get("by") or os.environ.get("COMMS_AGENT_ID") or "",
            "fixed": o.get("fixed", "")}
    call("friction_add", json.dumps(item, ensure_ascii=False))
    f = next((x for x in table("friction") if x["title"] == _line(title)[:160] and x["area"] == o["area"].strip().lower()), None)
    if f and o.get("task"):
        call("friction_link", f["id"], find(o["task"])["id"])
    print(f"{f['id']} x{f['count']}" if f else "logged")


# ---- the sweeper: what nobody is on, once, to the coordinator -------------------------------------------------------

SWEEP_GRACE_MS = 10 * 60_000   # a task this fresh (just added, just moved) isn't an orphan yet
ASK_GRACE_S = 10 * 60          # an ask the manager had 10 minutes to put on the board


def sweep_state_file():
    return os.environ.get("POWOS_SWEEP_STATE") or os.path.join(
        os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or os.path.expanduser("~/.local/state"), "powos", "board-sweep.json")


def orphans(ws, now_ms):
    """The rows nobody is on: stalled or no-check (a FAIL/INVALID/SKIP nobody picked up, a pass not closed, a fix
    with no check), and blocked ones without a reason; each past SWEEP_GRACE_MS since it last moved."""
    out = []
    for w in ws:
        moved = int(w.get("activity") or 0) or int(w.get("updated") or 0)
        if now_ms - moved < SWEEP_GRACE_MS:
            continue
        if w["truth"] in ("stalled", "no-check") or (w["truth"] == "blocked" and w["why"].endswith("no reason given")):
            out.append(w)
    return out


def _sig(*parts):
    return re.sub(r"\d+[smhd] ago", "", " | ".join(str(p) for p in parts))


QUIET_MS = 7 * 86400_000       # a one-off friction unseen this long goes quiet
STALE_QUEUE_MS = 86400_000     # a queued task nobody took in a day: listed as never picked up
SWEEP_PASSES = 5               # passes per sweep while one decided something and items remain
TOP_N = 10                     # the mail lists counts + this many by severity, never raw rows
REQUEUE_KINDS = ("plan", "failed", "dead-owner", "requeue")   # an orphan's decisions: each moves it to the queue
DEAD_OWNER_MS = 3600_000       # an owner with no live agent on a row that hasn't moved this long is a dead owner


def _norm_title(t):
    return " ".join(sorted(_words(t)))


def sweep_decide(ws, frictions, checks, asks, now_ms):
    """One pass's decisions over EVERYTHING (every open task, every open friction): a list of dicts {kind, id, why,
    calls: [(reducer, *args)]}. Pure: the caller applies the calls (or a dry run prints them). The dead-end states this
    resolves (each one a state nothing else moves):
      score    - its evidence says a different score/severity than stored: work_score (severity only rises)
      leaked   - a task whose last check PASSED holds planned steps that are another task's steps (a plan pasted into the
                 wrong task, so nothing ever closes it): those steps dropped from it (the other task keeps them)
      close    - open, nothing else open on it, and its latest deciding check is a PASS of a shipped build (an agent's or
                 the user's "works") or a recorded no-check reason, nobody holding it: closed done with that evidence
      merge    - an open task whose title is the same words as an older open one: merged into the older
      every orphan left (stalled / no-check / blocked without a reason) is DECIDED, never only listed: status queued
      (a picker sees it) with a why line, and a dead owner (not running, row unmoved DEAD_OWNER_MS - the coordinator
      too) cleared to "coder":
        plan       - its check PASSED but planned steps are left: flagged "plan leftover" (step names in the mail)
        failed     - its last check FAILED/INVALID/SKIPPED and nobody is on it: queued at its severity
        dead-owner - stalled, its owner isn't running
        requeue    - anything else nobody is on (a fix with no check, a PASS not closed, blocked with no reason)
      quiet    - a one-off friction (x1) unseen for 7 days: leaves the live list (reopens when logged again)
    Nothing is closed without evidence, and never over the user's own "still broken" verdict."""
    out = []
    open_ = [w for w in ws if w.get("status") != "done"]
    # The manager's own tasks (it builds some itself, e.g. the progress widget): never re-owned, closed, merged or
    # trimmed - only listed under "manager" in the mail (the manager, 11-01).
    mine = [w for w in open_ if (w.get("owner") or "") == "manager"]
    for w in mine:
        out.append({"kind": "manager", "id": w["id"], "why": "manager-owned: left alone", "calls": [], "quiet": True})
    by = checks_by_task(checks)
    for w in open_:
        ev = evidence(w["id"], frictions, checks, asks)
        sev = severity(w, ev)
        w["_ev"], w["severity"], w["score"], w["user_score"] = ev, sev, ev["score"], ev["user"]
        if (ev["score"], ev["user"], sev) != (int(w.get("_score0") or 0), int(w.get("_user0") or 0), int(w.get("_sev0") or 0)):
            out.append({"kind": "score", "id": w["id"], "why": f"score {ev['score']} -> {SEV_NAMES[sev] or 'none'}",
                        "calls": [("work_score", w["id"])], "quiet": True})
    # Scored above like every task; from here on the manager's own are left alone.
    open_ = [w for w in open_ if (w.get("owner") or "") != "manager"]
    # leaked plan steps: a planned step that is (exactly) a step of another open task
    texts = {}
    for w in open_:
        for x in _jl(w.get("steps", "")):
            if isinstance(x, dict) and _line(x.get("text", "")):
                texts.setdefault(_line(x["text"]).lower(), set()).add(w["id"])
    for w in open_:
        # Only on a task whose latest deciding check PASSED (the seen case: its own work passed, the plan holds steps
        # pasted from another task, so nothing ever closes it); the other task keeps them.
        res = sorted((c for c in by.get(w["id"], []) if c.get("state") in ("PASS", "FAIL", "none")), key=lambda c: int(c.get("at") or 0))
        if w.get("truth") == "working" or not res or res[-1]["state"] != "PASS":
            continue
        nxt = [_line(x.get("text", "")) for x in _jl(w.get("steps", "")) if isinstance(x, dict) and x.get("state") == "next"]
        # A generic word ("ship", "fixing") is many tasks' own step: only a specific line (3+ words) counts as leaked.
        leaked = list(dict.fromkeys(t for t in nxt if len(_words(t)) >= 3 and len(texts.get(t.lower(), ())) > 1))
        if leaked:
            keep = [t for t in nxt if t not in leaked]
            new = track(w, plan="; ".join(keep))
            w["steps"] = new["steps"] if new else w.get("steps", "")
            calls = [("work_track", w["id"], new["progress_done"], new["progress_total"], new["step"], new["steps"],
                      new["commits"], new["images"])] if new else []
            out.append({"kind": "leaked", "id": w["id"], "why": f"{len(leaked)} planned step(s) also on another task: "
                        + "; ".join(leaked)[:200], "calls": calls})
    for w in open_:
        if w.get("truth") in ("working", "awaiting-check") or w.get("status") in ("blocked", "waiting", "queued"):
            continue
        kids, steps = open_items(w, ws)
        if kids or steps:
            continue
        res = sorted((c for c in by.get(w["id"], []) if c.get("state") in ("PASS", "FAIL", "none")), key=lambda c: int(c.get("at") or 0))
        last = res[-1] if res else None
        # The user's own latest verdict "still broken" (check `you` FAIL) is never closed over, whatever passed since.
        mine_ = [c for c in res if c.get("name") == "you" and c.get("state") in ("PASS", "FAIL")]
        if mine_ and mine_[-1]["state"] == "FAIL":
            continue
        if last and ((last["state"] == "PASS" and last.get("shipped", True)) or (last["state"] == "none" and (last.get("line") or "").strip())):
            ev_ = (f"check {_check_name(last)} PASSED" if last["state"] == "PASS" else f"no device check: {last['line']}")[:200]
            out.append({"kind": "close", "id": w["id"], "why": ev_,
                        "calls": [("work_set", w["id"], "", "", "done", f"board sweep: closed on {ev_}"[:280], "")]})
            w["_closing"] = True
    seen = {}
    for w in sorted(open_, key=lambda w: (int(w.get("created") or 0), w["id"])):
        k = _norm_title(w["title"])
        if not k or w.get("_closing") or w.get("truth") == "working":
            continue
        if k in seen:
            out.append({"kind": "merge", "id": w["id"], "why": f"same title as {seen[k]}", "into": seen[k], "calls": []})
        else:
            seen[k] = w["id"]
    # Every orphan left (stalled / no-check / blocked without a reason, past the grace) gets a decision - a sweep that
    # only lists is broken (the user's rule, 11-01: for hours "Decided: nothing. orphans 65 -> 65" because only a
    # stalled task with an expert owner was ever "freed"; the coordinator's own, the FAILs and the PASS-with-plan-steps
    # rows had no decision at all). Each one goes to the queue (status queued) so a picker sees it, with a why line.
    taken = {d["id"] for d in out if d["kind"] in ("close", "merge", "leaked")}
    for w in orphans([w for w in open_ if w.get("truth") != "done"], now_ms):
        if w["id"] in taken or w.get("_closing"):
            continue
        owner = w.get("owner") or ""
        moved = int(w.get("activity") or 0) or int(w.get("updated") or 0)
        # Owner not running (no live agent of its role holds it - truth would be "working") and the row hasn't moved
        # in DEAD_OWNER_MS: a dead owner, cleared to "coder" (free) - the coordinator too: it staffs, it doesn't run it.
        dead = owner not in GENERIC_OWNERS and now_ms - moved >= DEAD_OWNER_MS
        new_owner = "coder" if dead else ""
        why0 = _line(w.get("why") or "")
        sev = SEV_NAMES.get(int(w.get("severity") or 0)) or "no severity"
        kids, steps = open_items(w, ws)
        res = sorted((c for c in by.get(w["id"], []) if c.get("state") in CHECK_RESULTS), key=lambda c: int(c.get("at") or 0))
        last = res[-1] if res else None
        if last and last["state"] == "PASS" and (steps or kids):
            # Its check PASSED but plan steps are left: a plan leftover - the coordinator decides next step vs drop;
            # meanwhile it waits in the queue for the picker of the next step.
            kind = "plan"
            why = f"plan leftover: check {_check_name(last)} PASSED, {open_why(kids, steps)} - queued for the next step"
        elif last and last["state"] in ("FAIL", "INVALID", "SKIP"):
            kind = "failed"
            why = f"check {_check_name(last)} {last['state']}, nobody on it - queued at {sev}"
        elif dead:
            kind = "dead-owner"
            why = f"owner {owner} isn't running ({ago(moved)} since it moved) - owner cleared, queued"
        else:
            kind = "requeue"
            why = f"nobody on it ({why0[:120]}) - queued at {sev}"
        if dead and kind != "dead-owner":
            why += f"; owner {owner} isn't running, cleared"
        out.append({"kind": kind, "id": w["id"], "why": why[:280], "steps": steps,
                    "calls": [("work_set", w["id"], "", new_owner, "queued", f"board sweep: {why}"[:280], "")]})
    for f in frictions:
        if f.get("status") == "open" and int(f.get("count") or 0) <= 1 and now_ms - int(f.get("last") or 0) >= QUIET_MS:
            out.append({"kind": "quiet", "id": f["id"], "why": f"x1, unseen {ago(int(f['last']))}", "calls": [("friction_quiet", f["id"])]})
    return out


def _board_facts(now_ms):
    ws = board_truth(now_ms=now_ms)
    for w in ws:   # what the module has stored, before this pass's recompute
        w["_score0"], w["_user0"], w["_sev0"] = w.get("score") or 0, w.get("user_score") or 0, w.get("severity") or 0

    def t(name):
        try:
            return table(name)
        except (Down, SystemExit):
            return []
    return ws, t("friction"), t("work_check"), t("user_ask")


def sweep(now_ms=None, mail=True, to="coder", full=False):
    """The board sweep (board-sweep.sh -> `powos agents sweep`, every 10 min): reads EVERYTHING each pass - every open
    task and every open friction - recomputes severity, resolves the dead-end states (sweep_decide), and when a pass
    decided something while orphans remain runs the next pass at once (up to SWEEP_PASSES). Then ONE bounded digest to
    [to] when something is new or changed: counts + the top TOP_N by severity. A dry run ([mail] False) decides one
    pass and applies nothing; [full]: the whole ranking with each task's score breakdown and every decision."""
    now_ms = now_ms or int(time.time() * 1000)
    try:
        if mail:   # a dry run writes nothing at all, not even the asks log
            sync_asks()
    except (Down, SystemExit):
        pass
    decided, passes, before, orph0 = [], 0, None, None
    while True:
        ws, frictions, checks, asks = _board_facts(now_ms)
        if before is None:
            before = (len([w for w in ws if w.get("status") != "done"]), len(orphans([w for w in ws if w["truth"] != "done"], now_ms)),
                      len([f for f in frictions if f.get("status") == "open"]))
        ds = sweep_decide(ws, frictions, checks, asks, now_ms)
        if orph0 is None:   # what nobody was on when the sweep started (scored by sweep_decide): the digest's list
            orph0 = orphans([w for w in ws if w["truth"] != "done"], now_ms)
        passes += 1
        if not mail:
            decided += ds
            break
        acted = 0
        for d in ds:
            try:
                if d["kind"] == "merge":
                    tgt = next(w for w in ws if w["id"] == d["into"])
                    merge_into(tgt, [next(w for w in ws if w["id"] == d["id"])], "board sweep: same title")
                else:
                    for c in d["calls"]:
                        call(*c)
            except SystemExit:   # a refusal (the module's done rule): left as it is, listed
                d["refused"] = True
                continue
            decided.append(d)
            acted += 0 if d.get("quiet") else 1
        remain = orphans([w for w in board_truth(now_ms=now_ms) if w["truth"] != "done"], now_ms)
        if not acted or not remain or passes >= SWEEP_PASSES:
            break
    ws, frictions, checks, asks = _board_facts(now_ms)
    for w in ws:   # a dry run's view: the recomputed severity (applied for real, it's the stored one now)
        ev = evidence(w["id"], frictions, checks, asks)
        w["_ev"], w["severity"], w["score"], w["user_score"] = ev, severity(w, ev), ev["score"], ev["user"]
    open_ = [w for w in ws if w["truth"] != "done"]
    sf = sweep_state_file()
    try:
        with open(sf) as f:
            prev = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        prev = {}
    seen = {"tasks": {}, "asks": {}, "friction": {}}
    new_tasks, new_asks, new_fr = [], [], []
    orph = orphans(open_, now_ms)
    for w in orph0:
        sig = _sig(w["truth"], w["why"], w.get("severity") or 0)
        seen["tasks"][w["id"]] = sig
        if prev.get("tasks", {}).get(w["id"]) != sig:
            new_tasks.append(w)
    for a in untracked_asks(ASK_GRACE_S):
        seen["asks"][a["id"]] = 1
        if a["id"] not in prev.get("asks", {}):
            new_asks.append(a)
    live_fr = [f for f in frictions if f["status"] == "open"]
    for f in live_fr:
        seen["friction"][f["id"]] = int(f["count"])
        if int(f["count"]) > int(prev.get("friction", {}).get(f["id"], 0)):
            new_fr.append(f)
    loud = [d for d in decided if not d.get("quiet")]
    after = (len([w for w in ws if w.get("status") != "done"]), len(orph), len(live_fr))
    if not mail:   # predicted: what applying the decisions would leave
        gone = {d["id"] for d in decided if d["kind"] in ("close", "merge")}
        moved = gone | {d["id"] for d in decided if d["kind"] in REQUEUE_KINDS}
        after = (before[0] - len(gone), len([w for w in orph if w["id"] not in moved]),
                 before[2] - sum(1 for d in decided if d["kind"] == "quiet"))
    stale_q = [w for w in open_ if w.get("status") == "queued" and now_ms - int(w.get("created") or now_ms) >= STALE_QUEUE_MS]
    digest = digest_text(open_, new_tasks, new_asks, new_fr, len(orph), len(seen["asks"]), loud, passes, before, after,
                         stale_q, sorted(orph0, key=rank_key), live_fr)
    if full:
        digest = (digest or digest_text(open_, [], [], [], len(orph), len(seen["asks"]), loud, passes, before, after,
                                        stale_q, sorted(orph0, key=rank_key), live_fr, force=True)) + full_text(open_, decided)
    mgr = [d["id"] for d in decided if d["kind"] == "manager"]
    if digest and mgr:   # the manager's own tasks: listed, never acted on (the manager, 11-01)
        digest += f"\n\nManager's own (left alone): {len(mgr)}: " + ", ".join(mgr[:10]) + (" ..." if len(mgr) > 10 else "")
    if digest and mail:
        r = subprocess.run((os.environ.get("POWOS_COMMS_CMD") or "powos comms").split()
                           + ["send", to, "-", "--from", "board-sweep"], input=digest, text=True, capture_output=True)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            die(f"sweep: mail to {to} failed: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    if mail:   # a dry run remembers nothing: the next real pass still mails what it showed
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(sf), exist_ok=True)
        with open(sf + ".tmp", "w") as f:
            json.dump(seen, f)
        os.replace(sf + ".tmp", sf)
    return digest


def _sev_tag(w):
    n = SEV_NAMES.get(int(w.get("severity") or 0), "")
    infra = " infra" if n and not int(w.get("user_score") or 0) else ""
    return f"{n}{infra} " if n else ""


def digest_text(open_, tasks, asks, fr, n_orphans, n_asks, decided=(), passes=1, before=None, after=None, stale_q=(),
                ranked=(), live_fr=(), force=False):
    if not (tasks or asks or fr or decided or force):
        return ""
    c = counts(open_)
    head = ", ".join(f"{c[s]} {s}" for s in TRUTH if s != "done" and c[s])
    out = [f"Board sweep: {len(tasks)} task(s), {len(asks)} ask(s), {len(fr)} friction new or changed "
           f"(open {len(open_)}: {head}; orphans {n_orphans}, asks without a task {n_asks}). Staff them: "
           f"`powos agents task set <id> --owner <expert>` + a fresh agent that claims it with --step."]
    if decided or before:
        kinds = {}
        for d in decided:
            kinds[d["kind"]] = kinds.get(d["kind"], 0) + 1
        out.append(f"Decided ({passes} pass{'es' if passes != 1 else ''}): "
                   + (", ".join(f"{n} {k}" for k, n in sorted(kinds.items())) or "nothing")
                   + (f". Open {before[0]} -> {after[0]}, orphans {before[1]} -> {after[1]}, live friction {before[2]} -> {after[2]}."
                      if before and after else ""))
    plans = [d for d in decided if d["kind"] == "plan"]
    if plans:
        out.append(f"Plan leftover (check PASSED, steps left; next step or drop them): {len(plans)}")
        for d in plans[:TOP_N]:
            out.append(f"- {d['id']}: " + "; ".join(d.get("steps") or [])[:200])
    if stale_q:
        out.append(f"Queued over a day, nobody took them: {len(stale_q)} (top: "
                   + ", ".join(w["id"] for w in sorted(stale_q, key=queue_key)[:5]) + ")")
    if ranked:
        out.append(f"\nTop {min(TOP_N, len(ranked))} of {len(ranked)} nobody was on (by severity, then reports, then age), "
                   f"each with this sweep's decision:")
        new_ids = {w["id"] for w in tasks}
        dec = {}
        for d in decided:
            dec.setdefault(d["id"], d["kind"])
        for w in list(ranked)[:TOP_N]:
            owner = f", owner {w['owner']}" if w.get("owner") else ""
            mark = " (new)" if w["id"] in new_ids else ""
            k = dec.get(w["id"])
            act = f" -> queued ({k})" if k in REQUEUE_KINDS else (f" -> {k}" if k else "")
            out.append(f"- {_sev_tag(w)}[{w['truth']}] {w['title']} ({w['id']}{owner}) - {_line(w['why'])[:200]}{mark}{act}")
    if asks:
        out.append(f"\nUser asks with no task ({len(asks)} new; manager: task add --ask <id>, or ask none <id> --reason):")
        for a in asks[:TOP_N]:
            out.append(f"- {a['id']} ({ago(int(a['at']))} ago): {_line(a['text'])[:200]}")
    if fr:
        frs = sorted(fr, key=lambda f: (-int(f["count"]), -int(f["last"])))
        out.append(f"\nFriction, new or recurring ({len(fr)}; live {len(live_fr)}; most frequent first; fix for good, then "
                   f"`powos friction fix <id> --commit`):")
        for f in frs[:TOP_N]:
            back = f", reopened x{f['reopened']}" if int(f.get("reopened") or 0) else ""
            on = f", task {f['task']}" if f.get("task") else ""
            out.append(f"- {f['id']} x{f['count']} [{f['area']}/{f['kind']}] {f['title']}{back}{on}"
                       + (f" - repro: {_line(f['repro'])[:160]}" if f.get("repro") else ""))
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def full_text(open_, decided):
    """--full: every open task ranked with its score breakdown, then every decision (the manager's review copy)."""
    out = ["\n== Severity ranking (score = friction x1 + still-broken x50 + repeated asks x25; P1 >= 50, P0 >= 500)"]
    for w in sorted(open_, key=rank_key):
        ev = w.get("_ev") or {"friction": 0, "broken": 0, "asks": 0, "score": 0, "user": 0}
        out.append(f"{_sev_tag(w) or '-  '}{ev['score']:>5}  friction {ev['friction']}, broken {ev['broken']}, asks {ev['asks']}"
                   f"  [{w['truth']}] {w['title']} ({w['id']})")
    out.append(f"\n== Decisions ({len(decided)})")
    for d in decided:
        into = f" into {d['into']}" if d.get("into") else ""
        out.append(f"{d['kind']:<7} {d['id']}{into} - {d['why']}" + (" (refused)" if d.get("refused") else ""))
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def _remote_run(argv, timeout=30):
    """One round-trip to the phone's module over the dev channel (powos-vadb). Returns (rc, stdout, stderr), or
    None if the attempt itself couldn't be made (no docker, or it timed out/erred before replying)."""
    if not shutil.which("docker"):
        return None
    b = base64.b64encode(json.dumps(argv).encode()).decode()
    inner = f"powos agents --argv-b64 {b}"
    cmd = ["docker", "exec", "powos-vadb", "adb", "shell", f"su -c \"sh /data/powos/powos-run.sh '{inner}'\""]
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(cmd, timeout=timeout, capture_output=True, text=True)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    return r.returncode, r.stdout, r.stderr


_UNKNOWN_ARGV_RE = re.compile(r"unknown option --|unknown: ")


def _stale_phone_stderr(rc, stderr):
    """None normally. If `stderr` looks like THIS script's own parse-error ("unknown option --x" / "unknown:
    verb") coming back from a remote run, that's suspicious: opts()/main() parse argv locally before ever
    touching the module, so the Mac itself already accepted this argv - a parse rejection can only come from
    an older copy running on the phone (f199/f170: f96 added `friction list --id` here; the phone's copy
    hadn't been redeployed, so the SAME flag came back "unknown"). Probe the phone's CLI_VERSION with one
    more round-trip and, if it's behind, return the clear replacement message instead of the confusing one."""
    if rc == 0 or not _UNKNOWN_ARGV_RE.search(stderr or ""):
        return None
    probe = _remote_run(["__cli_version__"])
    remote_v = 0   # couldn't even run __cli_version__ (even older than the probe itself): treat as 0
    if probe is not None:
        prc, pout, _ = probe
        if prc == 0:
            try:
                remote_v = int(pout.strip())
            except ValueError:
                remote_v = 0
    if remote_v < CLI_VERSION:
        return f"phone CLI is older (v{remote_v} < v{CLI_VERSION}): run rooted.sh deploy\n"
    return None


def remote(argv):
    """HACK: off the phone (the Mac's agents, the manager's coders) there is no local powos-agents module yet, so the
    command runs on the phone over the dev channel (powos-vadb). Real fix: each host's own module plus the Phase 2
    mirror (docs/AGENTS-VIEW-DESIGN.md §8), the hub merging hosts' boards."""
    out = _remote_run(argv)
    if out is None:
        return False
    rc, stdout, stderr = out
    stale = _stale_phone_stderr(rc, stderr)
    if stale is not None:
        sys.stderr.write(stale)
        sys.exit(rc)
    sys.stdout.write(stdout)
    sys.stderr.write(stderr)
    sys.exit(rc)


# ---- offline outbox (friction f61/f64): the board and friction live on the phone's SpacetimeDB (remote(), above),
# so both were unreachable - with no recovery - whenever the phone was off the VPN: a write just died, a read had
# nothing to fall back to, and remote()'s own docker-exec sat out its whole 30s timeout before failing. Writes now
# queue to a local outbox, in order, sent the next time anything checks in while the phone's reachable; reads fall
# back to the last cached board snapshot. phone_reachable() fails fast on adb.sh's own WireGuard-staleness check
# (sub-second) instead of waiting out a doomed round-trip every time.
OUTBOX_DIR = os.environ.get("POWOS_AGENTS_OUTBOX") or os.path.expanduser("~/.cache/powos-verify-queue/agents-outbox")
PENDING_DIR = os.path.join(OUTBOX_DIR, "pending")
CACHE_DIR = os.path.join(OUTBOX_DIR, "cache")
WRITE_VERBS = {
    ("task", "add"), ("task", "new"), ("task", "set"), ("task", "done"), ("task", "rm"), ("task", "infer"),
    ("check", "set"), ("check", "sync"), ("ask", "link"), ("ask", "none"), ("ask", "add"),
    ("friction", "add"), ("friction", "fix"), ("friction", "link"),
}


def is_write(argv):
    if not argv:
        return False
    if argv[0] == "units":
        return True   # units sync is the only verb, always a write
    return (argv[0], argv[1] if len(argv) > 1 else "") in WRITE_VERBS


def _cache_key(argv):
    return re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", "-".join(argv).lower()).strip("-") or "root"


def _adb_sh():
    override = os.environ.get("POWOS_AGENTS_ADB")
    if override:
        return override
    root = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
    return os.path.join(root, "tools", "phone", "adb.sh")


def phone_reachable():
    adb = _adb_sh()
    if not os.path.exists(adb):
        return True   # not the Mac (no adb.sh here, e.g. running ON the phone): let remote() try as before
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([adb, "--vpn-state"], capture_output=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return True   # unknown - don't invent an offline verdict we can't back up
    return r.returncode != 69


def outbox_enqueue(argv):
    os.makedirs(PENDING_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(PENDING_DIR, f"{time.time():020.6f}-{os.getpid()}.json")
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump({"argv": argv, "at": time.time()}, f)
    os.rename(tmp, path)


def outbox_pending():
    os.makedirs(PENDING_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    return sorted(os.path.join(PENDING_DIR, n) for n in os.listdir(PENDING_DIR) if n.endswith(".json"))


def outbox_flush():
    """Every queued write, oldest first, while the phone's reachable. Stops at the first one still unreachable
    (the phone dropped again mid-flush) - it and everything after it stay queued, in order."""
    if not phone_reachable():
        return
    for path in outbox_pending():
        try:
            with open(path) as f:
                item = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            os.remove(path)   # corrupt entry: never block the queue on it
            continue
        out = _remote_run(item["argv"])
        if out is None:
            break
        os.remove(path)


def cache_save(argv, text):
    os.makedirs(CACHE_DIR, exist_ok=True)
    path = os.path.join(CACHE_DIR, _cache_key(argv) + ".txt")
    tmp = path + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        f.write(text)
    os.rename(tmp, path)


def cache_load(argv):
    path = os.path.join(CACHE_DIR, _cache_key(argv) + ".txt")
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            text = f.read()
        when = time.strftime("%H:%M", time.localtime(os.path.getmtime(path)))
    except OSError:
        return None
    return text, when


def handle_down(argv):
    """The module isn't reachable locally (always true off the phone - remote()'s own HACK). Try the phone; off
    the VPN, queue a write for later or serve a read from the last cached snapshot - never just die."""
    outbox_flush()   # clear any backlog first, in order, so this call lands after whatever came before it
    if phone_reachable():
        out = _remote_run(argv)
        if out is not None:
            rc, stdout, stderr = out
            stale = _stale_phone_stderr(rc, stderr)
            if stale is not None:
                sys.stderr.write(stale)
                sys.exit(rc)
            sys.stdout.write(stdout)
            sys.stderr.write(stderr)
            if rc == 0 and not is_write(argv):
                cache_save(argv, stdout)
            sys.exit(rc)
    if is_write(argv):
        outbox_enqueue(argv)
        print("queued (offline): sent once the phone's back on the VPN")
        return 0
    cached = cache_load(argv)
    if cached:
        text, when = cached
        sys.stdout.write(text)
        print(f"(offline, as of {when})")
        return 0
    die(f"the powos-agents module isn't reachable at {SERVER} (phone offline, no cached board yet)")


def inline_stdin(argv):
    """`--details -`, `ask add -`, `check sync <file|->`: the text read HERE, into argv - the command may run on the
    phone (remote()), where neither this stdin nor this file is."""
    out = list(argv)
    for i, a in enumerate(out):
        if a == "-" and i > 0 and (out[i - 1] == "--details" or out[:2] == ["ask", "add"]):
            out[i] = sys.stdin.read()
    if out[:2] == ["check", "sync"] and len(out) == 3:
        out[2:] = ["--json-text", sys.stdin.read() if out[2] == "-" else open(out[2]).read()]
    return out


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["--argv-b64"] and len(argv) == 2:
        argv = json.loads(base64.b64decode(argv[1]))
    if argv == ["__cli_version__"]:
        # Answered locally, no module/network access - so it works on a phone copy even when its own
        # powos-agents module is unreachable, and works on an old copy too (it'll just be the old number).
        print(CLI_VERSION)
        return 0
    if not argv or argv[0] in ("help", "--help", "-h"):
        print(HELP, end="")
        return 0
    if argv[0] in ("task", "tasks", "work"):
        if len(argv) > 1 and argv[1] in ("help", "--help", "-h"):
            print(HELP, end="")
            return 0
        argv = argv[:1] + resolve_commits(argv[1:])
        try:
            task(argv[1:])
        except Down as e:
            if os.environ.get("POWOS_AGENTS_REMOTE", "1") == "0":
                die(f"the powos-agents module isn't reachable at {SERVER} ({e})")
            return handle_down(argv)
        return 0
    argv = inline_stdin(argv)
    sub = {"check": check_cmd, "checks": check_cmd, "ask": ask_cmd, "asks": ask_cmd, "friction": friction_cmd}
    if argv[0] in sub or argv[0] == "sweep":
        if argv[0] == "check" and argv[1:2] == ["scan"]:
            check_cmd(argv[1:])   # local: the Mac's queue dir
            return 0
        if argv[0] == "friction" and argv[1:2] in (["help"], ["--help"], ["-h"], []):
            print(FRICTION_HELP, end="")
            return 0
        try:
            if argv[0] == "sweep":
                o, _ = opts(argv[1:], ["dry-run!", "to", "full!"])
                d = sweep(mail=not o.get("dry-run"), to=o.get("to") or "coder", full=bool(o.get("full")))
                print(d or "board sweep: nothing new")
            else:
                sub[argv[0]](argv[1:])
        except Down as e:
            if os.environ.get("POWOS_AGENTS_REMOTE", "1") == "0":
                die(f"the powos-agents module isn't reachable at {SERVER} ({e})")
            return handle_down(argv)
        return 0
    if argv[0] == "units":
        # powos units publish: one host's units (lib/apps/powos-units snapshot) replace that host's rows in the `unit`
        # table, which the PowOS AI page lists. argv: units sync <base64 of {"host", "units": [...]}>.
        if len(argv) != 3 or argv[1] != "sync":
            die("usage: powos agents units sync <base64 JSON> (powos units publish writes it)")
        try:
            body = json.loads(base64.b64decode(argv[2]))
            call("unit_sync", body["host"], json.dumps(body["units"], separators=(",", ":")))
        except Down as e:
            if os.environ.get("POWOS_AGENTS_REMOTE", "1") == "0":
                die(f"the powos-agents module isn't reachable at {SERVER} ({e})")
            return handle_down(argv)
        except (ValueError, KeyError) as e:
            die(f"units sync: {e}")
        return 0
    die(f"unknown: {argv[0]} (powos agents help)")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]) or 0)
